+# Tool input validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+Tool definitions already describe the input that providers ask models to produce. The registry is the enforcement boundary, so malformed calls return corrective tool results and never reach application executors.
+
+## Registry contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates required fields and declared types before the executor runs; a rejected call returns a result that identifies the failing path and constraint without exposing input values. ([validated by: validates malformed input safely while preserving valid extra properties](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L10))
+- A schema-valid call preserves unlisted properties exactly as supplied and invokes its executor once. ([validated by: validates malformed input safely while preserving valid extra properties](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L10))
+- Registering a static definition rejects an uncompilable schema immediately and names the tool in the error. ([validated by: rejects an invalid static schema when registering the named tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L43))
+- A function-valued definition is validated against the schema it returns for each call. ([validated by: uses the current schema returned by a dynamic definition](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L54))
+- A static definition keeps its validator compiled at registration for later executions. ([validated by: keeps using the schema compiled at static registration across executions](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L85))
